+/* Restyling for a change of state (VitaSurf)                               */
+
+/*
+ * An element that becomes :hover, :focus, :active or :target is selected
+ * again on its own rather than the whole tree being rebuilt, which on
+ * the Vita can take a second. When all that changed is paint -- colours,
+ * a background, an outline, a shadow -- the new styles are put on the
+ * boxes the element owns and the page is drawn again; when something
+ * would move, the caller rebuilds the layout instead.
